---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-26-bring-what-you-have.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-26',
  title: 'New workflow page: Bring What You Already Have',
  tags: ['workflows', 'import', 'contracts', 'applications', 'seo'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added a Bring What You Already Have workflow page at
    <a href="/workflows/bring-what-you-have" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/bring-what-you-have</a>.
    It covers four routes for a breeder switching to BreederHQ: importing records with Scout, keeping their own contract
    with Fill &amp; Sign or contract import, importing an existing application form as a screening template, and taking
    applications from their website with Application Links. It states that an existing Stripe account cannot be connected directly.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">New file</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><code>src/pages/workflows/bring-what-you-have.astro</code>: the four routes, what each one reads, what the breeder reviews before anything is saved, and what does not carry over. Includes FAQPage and HowTo structured data.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">SEO</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The new page is picked up by the generated sitemap on the next build. Navigation, the workflows index, and the sibling pages for each route are linked in a follow-up. No screenshots yet; they follow separately.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
